comments.body:
Would it possible to add a method (get_any_connection) in mavsdk api which allow you to get a reference to the connection instance itself i.e. 

std::shared_ptr<Connection>& connection = mavsdk.get_any_connection(const std::string& connection_url);

Then the programmer can call connection.stop(); and connection.start(); to deconstruct and construct the connection again without deleting all instances of classes already created?

Edit: or have two new methods in mavsdk i.e.

mavsdk.stop_any_connection(const std::string& connection_url);
mavsdk.start_any_connection(const std::string& connection_url);

